<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.74 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.74 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state Cotton Export Corporation (CEC) said on Friday that Pakistan's 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.742 million 375-lb bales by Thursday, down from 9.944 million in the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.658 (8.173)  2.084 (1.770)  8.742 (9.944)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.653 (8.171)  2.084 (1.770)  8.737 (9.941)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.916 (6.919)  1.916 (1.272)  7.832 (8.191)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.008 (1.023)  0.012 (0.471)  0.020 (1.494)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   0.733 (0.229)  0.155 (0.027)  0.889 (0.257)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
